l_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=4\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55d7b8eab4c0b404bb3a58086a708d6522cfbf70992c0717bb08f606c61703ad"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] ["math" "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327992" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=5,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "55d7b8eab4c0b404bb3a58086a708d6522cfbf70992c0717bb08f606c61703ad"} {"question" "q-327998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9a7ed6687ee7be2"} {"question" "q-327998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069460/state.json" "file_sha256" "db0f04a6d3105bd6548c6856d8eded0fc6b67f27cb5af6f5c9